This slide shows the operator view of the PoC.

An enterprise team can configure the model, thresholds, policy corpus, and run mode from the dashboard.

The workflow starts when the target GenAI app is submitted for pre-production evaluation.

Gemini then creates failure-seeking prompts across categories like hallucination, PII extraction, jailbreak attempts, toxicity, and policy-risk scenarios.

For example, the system can test whether the assistant exposes employee details, follows a malicious instruction, or gives an unauthorized policy decision.

Google ADK routes each response to the right safety tool. Groundedness checks whether the answer is supported by source documents. PII scanning checks whether sensitive identifiers appear. Toxicity scoring checks whether the response is safe and appropriate.

If thresholds fail, deployment is blocked. Then the system moves to remediation, hardens the prompt, re-runs the tests, and approves only after measurable recovery.

This makes responsible AI visible, measurable, and actionable.

