## Slide 9 — Proof of Execution

**Time: 1 minute 10 seconds**

This is the strongest evidence point because it shows how the solution ran end-to-end on the Google platform.

The PoC used a Google-based execution flow:

First, the synthetic HR policy documents were loaded and indexed for RAG grounding.
Then the evaluation workflow built the retrieval context.
Gemini generated adversarial test prompts.
The target HR Policy Assistant was tested with those prompts.
The ADK evaluator agent called the safety tools for groundedness, toxicity, and PII checks.
The release gate applied the configured thresholds.
When the app failed, Gemini generated hardened prompt guidance.
Then the evaluation was run again to validate recovery.

So this is not just a static report. It is a working pipeline: **load docs, build RAG, generate tests, execute, evaluate, gate, remediate, and re-test**.

In the documented PoC run, the first evaluation was blocked. Groundedness was **0.840**, below the required **0.850** threshold, and there were **8 active failures**.

After remediation, groundedness improved to **0.942**, toxicity to **0.970**, and PII protection to **0.992**. Active failures reduced from **8 to 0** in the documented PoC run.

I am not claiming every real-world system will always show complete recovery. The important point is that the PoC proves a repeatable safety workflow: detect the risk, block the release, diagnose the issue, harden the system, re-test, and approve only after measurable improvement.

