## Slides 11 and 12 — Security, Scale, and Business Value

**Time: 1 minute**

The solution supports four responsible AI guardrails.

First, **PII and data privacy**, through multi-pattern sensitive-data detection.

Second, **grounding and citations**, by checking answers against enterprise source documents.

Third, **auditability**, by storing scores, thresholds, verdicts, timestamps, remediation history, and operator evidence.

Fourth, **domain boundaries**, by rejecting role overrides, unauthorized approvals, and unsupported responses.

The release policy is deterministic: groundedness, toxicity, PII protection, category floors, and critical failures all have to pass.

This helps AI deployment teams, compliance teams, risk teams, security teams, and business owners.

From a business perspective, the value is threefold.

It reduces manual red-team effort.
It catches risk before production.
And it creates audit-ready evidence for governance.

The same pattern can extend beyond the HR PoC to BFSI assistants, compliance copilots, customer support, legal workflows, and other regulated GenAI use cases.

For TCS, this can become a reusable **GenAI Safety-as-a-Service accelerator**.

In enterprise AI, **trust is not a feature. Trust is the product.**

